    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d402">

                <pb facs="0815" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg801"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Willey, district
                        attorney, to Mr. Field, Assistant
                        Attorney-General.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New London,
                        Connecticut</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1869-07-01"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 1, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. A. Field</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Assistant Attorney-General, Washington:</hi></p>
                <p>Your telegram is received. I have telegraphed the marshal at New Haven to proceed
                    at once to Milford, to hold the schooners Fancy and Winona, their arms,
                    ammunition, and men, in custody till further orders. The enlistment of men was
                    in the southern district of New York, and should be presented in that
                    district.</p>
                <p><seg type="margin">[85]</seg> Is it the purpose of the Government to libel *the
                    vessel and cargo as forfeited? If so, instruct me to do so.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HIRAM WILLEY,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States
                        Attorney.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
